00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:23.440
So carry a picture of a coyote

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:25.320
next time you walking past.

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:26.340
Just the other night.

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:27.173
Oh no.

00:10:27.173 --> 00:10:28.006
Is this bad?

00:10:28.006 --> 00:10:29.510
Jesse and I are walking.

00:10:29.510 --> 00:10:31.920
Getting ready to get up to the house,

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:36.440
get to the house on the
post in front of the house,

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:38.250
there is a sign.

00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:39.350
What?

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:40.640
It is a picture of my friend.

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:42.503
And it says lost cat.

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:45.093
You stole the cat.

00:10:45.093 --> 00:10:47.460
I did not steal the damn cat.

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:48.700
The cat is gone.

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:50.250
Oh no.

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:53.540
And, uh--
Both halves?

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:55.440
I'm assuming.

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:56.273
The cat's gone.

00:10:56.273 --> 00:10:57.806
And then I, then on the rest of our walk--

00:10:57.806 --> 00:10:59.658
The cat didn't have a collar.

00:10:59.658 --> 00:11:01.358
The cat didn't have a collar!

00:11:01.358 --> 00:11:02.633
I noticed--

00:11:02.633 --> 00:11:03.466
Did people make--
Other signs--

00:11:03.466 --> 00:11:04.990
A sign for a cat?

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:07.100
If you care enough to make
a sign when the cat is gone,

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:09.080
you should care enough
to give the cat a collar

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:10.340
before it's gone.

00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:12.590
I just think this cat
didn't need a collar.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:15.340
But anyway, there's other signs

00:11:15.340 --> 00:11:17.400
all throughout the neighborhood.

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:18.270
Dang.

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:21.490
And I was just like, what does this mean?

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:22.960
I don't really believe that the universe

00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:27.020
is telling me things, but I
do find it somewhat helpful

00:11:27.020 --> 00:11:30.830
to just assume the universe
is telling me things.

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:32.430
I find that a useful way to live.

00:11:32.430 --> 00:11:34.560
If God, I'm gonna to say, God--

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:35.393
Sure. I think that's interchangeable--.

00:11:35.393 --> 00:11:36.226
is gonna tell you something.

00:11:36.226 --> 00:11:37.190
I think that's interchangeable
with the term "Universe."

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:38.050
For you?

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:40.993
Then he's gonna tell you something.

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:45.070
I hope it's gonna be, not about a cat.

00:11:45.070 --> 00:11:46.057
Well, I mean--

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:50.740
If the universe is telling
you something, what is it?

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:52.090
And why is this about you?

00:11:52.090 --> 00:11:53.730
I'm just, well, because I'm--

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:55.130
Somebody lost a poor cat.

00:11:55.130 --> 00:11:57.470
I'm interacting with this cat, so--

00:11:57.470 --> 00:11:58.303
Okay.

00:11:58.303 --> 00:11:59.780
In my world and my point of reference--

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:01.030
Okay.
I need to understand,

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:02.860
that's a weird question to ask.

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:05.863
I'm just messing with you.

00:12:07.420 --> 00:12:11.763
I'm trying to figure out how
I should interpret this sign.

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:15.330
You know, I was moving towards a cat.

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:17.523
I was opening my heart towards a cat.

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:20.263
I was enjoying time with cat.

00:12:22.432 --> 00:12:23.274
And...

00:12:23.274 --> 00:12:24.820
And, and now cat has gone.

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:25.830
Cat was taken from you.

00:12:25.830 --> 00:12:28.653
And listen, I listen, I
feel for these people,

00:12:29.650 --> 00:12:30.820
but that cat is dead.

00:12:30.820 --> 00:12:33.370
I mean, I interacted
with that cat long enough

00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:35.830
to know that that cat in our neighborhood,

00:12:35.830 --> 00:12:37.300
that cat is not around anymore.

00:12:37.300 --> 00:12:38.490
You thought, but--

00:12:38.490 --> 00:12:39.323
I mean, maybe somebody did steal it--

00:12:39.323 --> 00:12:41.120
You did say, for a second.

00:12:41.120 --> 00:12:43.190
You thought, I'd like,
I wouldn't like a cat.

00:12:43.190 --> 00:12:44.320
I would like this cat.

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:47.580
And I will, in one time,
Barbara got out of our house,

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:51.840
you know the story she, she
literally, somebody stopped

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:53.130
and saw her walking down the street.

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:54.870
They opened the door and she
jumped in the car with them.

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:57.150
That is the kind of dog that Barbara is.

00:12:57.150 --> 00:12:59.560
And that's the kind of
cat that this cat was.

00:12:59.560 --> 00:13:01.370
So it's a lover.

00:13:01.370 --> 00:13:02.220
It's not a fighter.

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:04.350
And so it will, it tried to love a coyote.

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:08.053
And I think the coyote gave it
a special kind of love back.

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:12.630
Again the collar thing
reduces the level of sympathy.

00:13:12.630 --> 00:13:16.940
But I do know that there
are people who will feed

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:20.190
feral cats and they will consider it,

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:21.700
they will have a relationship with them,

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:22.533
but they won't--
Well yeah--

00:13:22.533 --> 00:13:23.600
Let them in the house, they won't--

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:26.360
This is clearly that kind of relationship.

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:28.280
Yeah, we had a guy who was
moving out of our neighborhood,

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:30.590
who was friends with
Christie, through the gym

00:13:30.590 --> 00:13:32.710
she used to go to and he was like, listen,

00:13:32.710 --> 00:13:36.370
I know you guys live near
me, a couple of streets

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:38.070
down the hill.

00:13:38.070 --> 00:13:40.283
This is an odd request, but we're moving.

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:42.233
Do you want our cat?

00:13:42.233 --> 00:13:43.070
Would you--

00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:44.120
Would you feed our cat?

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:45.960
Yeah. Would you take care of our cat?

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:47.840
Cause it's a, it's a feral cat.

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:49.220
It just, it runs through the neighborhood,

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:51.760
but we feed it and she
shows up every morning

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:53.080
and I wanna bring her to your house

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:54.170
and have you feed her and have her

00:13:54.170 --> 00:13:55.700
start showing up at your door?

00:13:55.700 --> 00:13:57.730
Like he was really
concerned about this cat.

00:13:57.730 --> 00:13:58.694
Hmm. You said no?

00:13:58.694 --> 00:14:00.640
And I guess, you know, you
can't have it both ways.

00:14:00.640 --> 00:14:03.860
I would think it would
be weird if that cat,

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:05.770
a feral cat, who you just happened to feed

00:14:05.770 --> 00:14:09.410
and have a relationship
with, when it goes missing,

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:11.523
you would put up signs to then what?

00:14:12.640 --> 00:14:13.527
Bring it back so you--

00:14:13.527 --> 00:14:15.490
So it will come back.

00:14:15.490 --> 00:14:17.600
But it goes off, it's a free cat.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:18.433
That cat--

00:14:18.433 --> 00:14:19.290
Well, hold on.

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:20.123
The short life it lives--

00:14:20.123 --> 00:14:21.600
I'm not a cat expert--

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:22.950
Was a full life, man.

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:24.300
I'm not a cat expert, but I--

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:25.660
That cat!
I tend to believe,

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:30.660
that feral cats in the,
in the traditional sense

00:14:30.710 --> 00:14:34.823
are not as people, they
don't come up to people--

00:14:34.823 --> 00:14:35.656
That is strange, yeah.

00:14:35.656 --> 00:14:36.850
And meow--
Yeah, that's strange.

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:37.683
And rub on them, this is a house cat.

00:14:37.683 --> 00:14:41.280
This is a cat that has it both ways.

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:43.520
This is a cat that gets whatever it wants.

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:46.160
This cat definitely was on
the inside and the outside.

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:47.123
And you know what?

00:14:47.123 --> 00:14:49.189
This is like a cat in a halfway house.

00:14:49.189 --> 00:14:50.022
You know what I'm saying?

00:14:50.022 --> 00:14:51.520
I think we can celebrate the cat's life.

00:14:51.520 --> 00:14:53.240
And we don't have to feel sad because--

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:54.073
Halfway house that is a--

00:14:54.073 --> 00:14:55.470
That cat had it all.

00:14:55.470 --> 00:14:57.310
Half. He's in half right now.

00:14:57.310 --> 00:14:59.760
That cat everyone, it met.

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:02.600
It just, it just showered with love.

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:03.750
I mean, no offense to you.

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:04.756
I don't think you were special--

00:15:04.756 --> 00:15:06.010
It lived a full life.

00:15:06.010 --> 00:15:06.843
In that sense.

00:15:06.843 --> 00:15:08.330
No, it ended up, it ended up developing

00:15:08.330 --> 00:15:09.163
a special bond with me.

00:15:09.163 --> 00:15:11.540
You were a giant dude walking a dog.

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:13.810
If it came up to you, that
cat would come up to anything.

00:15:13.810 --> 00:15:14.643
You're right.

00:15:14.643 --> 00:15:16.291
It would come out to a coyote.

00:15:16.291 --> 00:15:17.970
My dog does the same thing.

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:20.503
My dog has no loyalty to
me and I still love it.

00:15:21.970 --> 00:15:23.993
My dog would have gone home
and just started a new life

00:15:23.993 --> 00:15:25.130
with that other family.

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:26.250
I know it for a fact.

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:27.083
So you--

00:15:27.083 --> 00:15:27.916
Never thought about us again.

00:15:27.916 --> 00:15:29.830
Okay, well maybe that
cat, did you name it?

00:15:29.830 --> 00:15:30.900
It has a name.

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:33.313
And it's on the sign, but I
didn't wanna say it because--

00:15:33.313 --> 00:15:34.146
I don't want to--
Oh!

00:15:34.146 --> 00:15:35.690
You know, I don't like people
making connections with it.

00:15:35.690 --> 00:15:37.500
It had a name, but it
didn't have a collar.

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:39.770
With the neighborhood
and that kinda thing.

00:15:39.770 --> 00:15:40.640
It still doesn't add up.

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:42.550
I don't think I'm missing anything, am I?

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:44.200
It's just doesn't

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:45.033
I think it's pretty simple.

00:15:45.033 --> 00:15:47.410
You gonna post signs when it's gone,

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:50.210
you need to give it a
collar before it leaves.

00:15:50.210 --> 00:15:51.136
Yeah.

00:15:51.136 --> 00:15:54.020
I think the cat is just, was a loose,

00:15:54.020 --> 00:15:55.760
they were holding onto
this cat very loosely

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:56.593
and they lost grip.

00:15:56.593 --> 00:15:59.600
But for you the cat was
an angel leading you

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:01.790
to the love of the feline.

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:03.750
I didn't know where the
relationship was going,

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:05.580
but it was going places very fast.

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:07.670
And I was just letting my heart.

00:16:07.670 --> 00:16:08.690
just take flight.

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:10.960
I wasn't--
It ended all too soon.

00:16:10.960 --> 00:16:14.070
I was rerouting my path to this house.

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:15.513
I was spending quality time with the cat.

00:16:15.513 --> 00:16:17.860
I was getting pictures with the cat.

00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:18.693
Hmm--

00:16:18.693 --> 00:16:20.670
Are you okay? I don't
wanna gloss over that.

00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:21.920
I don't think I'm okay.

00:16:24.010 --> 00:16:26.030
Because I don't think I'll
find another cat like this.

00:16:26.030 --> 00:16:27.680
You won't.
I know for a fact,

00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:28.890
I mean, first of all,

00:16:28.890 --> 00:16:31.760
if you don't like kittens,
you don't have a heart.

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:33.410
You're not human if
you don't like kittens,

00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:35.220
like no-one's like, kittens suck. Right?

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:37.683
Kittens are awesome. I
got to have a kitten.

00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:42.420
But the chances that the kitten
turns into a regular cat,

00:16:42.420 --> 00:16:43.670
Pretty high.
So high.

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:46.135
So high.
And at that point it's like

00:16:46.135 --> 00:16:48.426
I'm not interested anymore.

00:16:48.426 --> 00:16:52.690
I want the animal to love me.

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:55.550
I'm getting emotional
support from this animal.

00:16:55.550 --> 00:16:57.280
I mean, when I do my
stretches in the morning

00:16:57.280 --> 00:16:59.320
and Barbara gets on me.

00:16:59.320 --> 00:17:01.950
I need that. I become dependent upon that.

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:02.783
You know what I'm saying?

00:17:02.783 --> 00:17:04.820
When Barbara leaves or Barbara dies--

00:17:04.820 --> 00:17:05.653
Hmm.

00:17:05.653 --> 00:17:08.550
She will be replaced
potentially with a clone of her

00:17:08.550 --> 00:17:10.000
or probably just another dog.

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:15.700
A lot of responses to our
prompt of what question

00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:18.850
